# Blender outputs. Every .blend is regenerated by `blender/build_all.sh` from the
# .py sources, so the scripts are the source of truth and the .blend is a build
# artifact. Also note save_as_mainfile rotates cat.blend -> cat.blend1, so these
# churn on every single run.
*.blend
*.blend1

# Exploration renders. ~100MB of colourway/pattern/face studies from the design
# phase. The decisions they led to are recorded in CLAUDE.md and SPRITE_CONTRACT.md;
# the images themselves are regenerable by re-running the explore_*.py scripts.
blender/face/
blender/pattern/
blender/bw/
blender/style/
blender/palettes/
blender/eyecmp/
blender/web_sprites/
blender/*.png

# Review composites - regenerated by blender/make_previews.sh.
blender/previews/

# Derived from veo-output/loaf_veo.mp4 with ffmpeg. The mp4 itself IS tracked
# (a Veo run costs money to repeat); its frame grids are not.
veo-output/grid.png
veo-output/gait_row.png

# Local reference material - third-party repos cloned here for comparison, each
# carrying its own .git. Committing one would embed a repository inside this one.
ref/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Kept locally, not published. Everything below is history or a dev-only tool:
# none of it is needed to build the app, render a sprite, or understand the
# design. All of it stays on disk and remains in git history.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Design-phase Blender studies. CLAUDE.md §2 already calls these "History, not
# source" - the look they led to is locked into build_cat.py and §4.
blender/explore_*.py
blender/palette_sheet.py

# A compiled walk cycle for eyeballing motion without opening Blender. Handy
# locally, regenerable, and not part of the build.
blender/walk.gif

# Google Veo was evaluated as a sprite source and disqualified; ANALYSIS.md
# records why. Keeping 1.5MB of footage for an approach that was rejected is
# exactly the kind of weight this repo strips elsewhere.
veo-output/
veo-prompts.md

# Three.js live-rig previewer. A dev tool, explicitly not shipped, and 1.2MB of
# it is vendored three.js.
web/

# The original brain-dump, superseded by CLAUDE.md, and the working resumption
# note. Both are personal notes rather than project documentation.
Idea.md
CONTEXT.md

# Design-phase studies, kept locally but not published. Same rule as the
# exploration renders above: the decisions they led to are recorded in CLAUDE.md
# §4 and locked into build_cat.py, so the studies themselves are history rather
# than source. Recoverable from git history if ever needed.
behaviour-plan.html
coat-study.html
coat-study.src.html
colour-study.html
paw-drop-study.html

# Generated by tools/build_showcase.py from loaf-showcase.src.html plus whatever
# is currently in Resources/sprites. ~6MB of embedded base64, and regenerating it
# is one command - tracking it would mean re-committing 6MB every art change.
loaf-showcase.html

# Which GitHub account to push this repo with, and the emails not to use. Split
# out of CLAUDE.md §1 when the repo went public - it is personal account detail,
# useful locally and nobody else's business. CLAUDE.md §1 points at it.
.git-identity.md

# Credentials. Nothing here has ever been committed, and this is here to keep it
# that way: the documented way to give her a key is LOAF_OPENROUTER_KEY, so the
# obvious next step for anyone running her is a .env, which would otherwise be
# committed on the very next `git add -A`.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.keystore
secrets.*
credentials.*

__pycache__/
*.pyc

# SwiftPM
.build/
dist/
*.xcodeproj
.swiftpm/

.DS_Store

# Blender writes sprites into the Swift package (Sources/Loaf/Resources/sprites),
# and those ARE tracked - they are the app's assets. Only the review composites,
# which make_previews.sh regenerates, are not.
